seekserve's patch to libtorrent (app BUG-202), applied by the top CMakeLists.txt
before libtorrent is built, on top of the submodule's commit.

part_file::export_file: a slot of the part file may hold only the part of a
piece that belongs to another file. That happens when the piece came while this
file was wanted (its part went to its own file) and the other file was not (its
part went to the part file). If this file is then deleted, a check of the torrent
moves it to the part file (mmap_storage::initialize: a file with priority 0 that
does not exist uses the part file), and wanting it again copies its pieces out of
the part file (mmap_storage::set_file_priority). Reading this file's part of such
a slot reached the end of the part file: "End of file", and the torrent went into
error, paused, with its file priorities unchanged. Nothing of this file is in that
slot: nothing to copy, and the piece, which the check found missing, comes again.

